#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How Ditana probes your system at install time and adapts configurations transparently, with all detection logic centralized in one auditable file."
msgstr "Co che Ditana examinescha Voss sistem durant l’installaziun ed adatta las configuraziuns en moda transparenta, cun l’entira logica d’identificaziun centralisada en ina suletta datoteca controllabla."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware detection"
msgstr "Identificaziun da la hardware"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"A traditional installer offers you the same dialogs regardless of whether "
"your laptop has an Intel iGPU or an NVIDIA card; whether you're on bare "
"metal or in a VM; whether your CPU is affected by RETBleed or not. You're "
"expected to know."
msgstr ""
"In installatur tradiziunal As porscha ils medems dialogs, independentamain "
"da sche Voss laptop ha in’iGPU dad Intel u ina carta NVIDIA; sche Vus "
"lavurais directamain sin la hardware u en ina VM; sche Vossa CPU è "
"pertutgada da RETBleed u betg. I vegn spetgà che Vus sappias quai."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Ditana adapts the dialogs to your hardware. Choices you don't need are "
"hidden or pre-filled with safe defaults; choices you do need surface with "
"sensible recommendations."
msgstr ""
"Ditana adatta ils dialogs a Vossa hardware. Tschernas che Vus na duvrais "
"betg vegnan zuppadas u emplenidas ordavant cun valurs da standard segiras; "
"tschernas che Vus duvrais cumparan cun recumandaziuns raschunaivlas."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The detection principle"
msgstr "Il princip da l’identificaziun"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"All probing that feeds the knowledge base lives in a single file: [`hardware-"
"detection.kdl`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/blob/main/settings/"
"hardware-detection.kdl). Each detector is one line of Raku that runs once at "
"installer startup and exposes a value – usually a boolean – to the rest of "
"the knowledge base. Probing that needs more than a line lives in the "
"installer engine: the graphics card is matched against the lists NVIDIA "
"publishes, and the NVMe block format, rotational media and the EFI partition "
"are found there too."
msgstr ""
"L’entira examinaziun che furnescha datas a la basa da savida sa chatta en "
"ina suletta datoteca: [`hardware-detection.kdl`](https://github.com/acrion/"
"ditana-config/blob/main/settings/hardware-detection.kdl). Mintga detectur è "
"ina lingia da Raku che vegn exequida ina giada a l’aviar da l’installatur e "
"metta a disposiziun dal rest da la basa da savida ina valur – per il solit "
"ina valur booleana. Examinaziuns che dovran dapli ch’ina lingia sa chattan "
"en il motor da l’installatur: là vegn la carta da grafica cumparegliada cun "
"las glistas che NVIDIA publitgescha, e là vegnan er chattads il format da "
"blocs NVMe, ils discs rotativs e la partiziun EFI."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid "A few representative examples from the live file:"
msgstr "Intgins exempels represchentativs da la datoteca en diever:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"uefi\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/sys/firmware/efi'.IO.e\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"intel-cpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/proc/cpuinfo'.IO.lines.first(* ~~ /vendor_id/).contains('GenuineIntel')\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"virtual-environment\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"run('systemd-detect-virt', '-q').exitcode eq 0\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"is-retbleed-vulnerable\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given '/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/retbleed'.IO\n"
"            { .e && .slurp.chomp ne 'Not affected' }\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"uefi\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/sys/firmware/efi'.IO.e\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"intel-cpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/proc/cpuinfo'.IO.lines.first(* ~~ /vendor_id/).contains('GenuineIntel')\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"virtual-environment\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"run('systemd-detect-virt', '-q').exitcode eq 0\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"is-retbleed-vulnerable\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given '/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/retbleed'.IO\n"
"            { .e && .slurp.chomp ne 'Not affected' }\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Each one reads from `/sys/`, `/proc/`, or shells out to a standard tool — no "
"proprietary hardware abstraction layer, no opaque database. If you want to "
"know *what* Ditana detects and *how*, the answer fits on one screen and you "
"don't need to leave the file."
msgstr ""
"Mintga detectur legia da `/sys/`, `/proc/` u cloma in utensil standard – "
"nagin nivel d’abstracziun da la hardware proprietar, nagina banca da datas "
"opaca. Sche Vus vulais savair *tge* che Ditana identifitgescha e *co*, ha la "
"resposta plaz sin in sulet visur, e Vus na stuais betg bandunar la datoteca."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "From detection to decision"
msgstr "Da l’identificaziun a la decisiun"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Detectors don't act on their own. They expose values that other settings "
"reference in their `default-value` or `available` expressions. The chain is "
"always: **detect → decide → install**."
msgstr ""
"Ils detecturs n’ageschan betg sezs. Els mettan a disposiziun valurs, a las "
"qualas auters parameters fan referenza en lur expressiuns `default-value` u "
"`available`. La chadaina è adina: **identifitgar → decider → installar**."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"A clean example is CPU vulnerability mitigation. Each kernel-reported "
"vulnerability (Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, TAA, MMIO Stale Data, L1TF, "
"RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS) has its own detector. The corresponding "
"mitigation setting then references that detector as its default:"
msgstr ""
"In exempel cler è la mitigiaziun da mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU. Mintga "
"mancanza da segirezza che il kernel annunzia (Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, "
"TAA, MMIO Stale Data, L1TF, RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS) ha ses agen detectur. "
"Il parameter da mitigiaziun correspundent fa lura referenza a quest detectur "
"sco sia valur da standard:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"kernel-option-retbl\" \\\n"
"  dialog-name=\"CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options\" \\\n"
"  short-description=\"Enforce Retbleed Mitigation (retbleed=auto,nosmt)\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`is-retbleed-vulnerable`\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"kernel-option-retbl\" \\\n"
"  dialog-name=\"CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options\" \\\n"
"  short-description=\"Enforce Retbleed Mitigation (retbleed=auto,nosmt)\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`is-retbleed-vulnerable`\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"If your CPU isn't affected, the checkbox starts unchecked. If it is, it "
"starts checked. Nothing is filtered by CPU: every mitigation is listed "
"either way, so you can also see what your CPU was found not to need. The one "
"thing that does remove them from the dialog is choosing `mitigations=off`, "
"which makes each of them pointless — see [how settings depend on each other]"
"(/under-the-hood/settings-logic/). See the [CPU mitigations page](/under-the-"
"hood/mitigations/) for the full per-vulnerability rationale."
msgstr ""
"Sche Vossa CPU n’è betg pertutgada, è la chaschetta da controlla deactivada "
"sco standard. Sch’ella è pertutgada, è la chaschetta activada sco standard. "
"Nagut na vegn filtrà tenor la CPU: mintga mitigiaziun vegn mussada en mintga "
"cas, uschia che Vus pudais er vesair tge che Vossa CPU, tenor "
"l’identificaziun, na dovra betg. La suletta chaussa che las allontanescha "
"dal dialog è la tscherna da `mitigations=off`, che las renda tuttas inutilas "
"– guardai [co ch’ils parameters dependan l’in da l’auter](/under-the-hood/"
"settings-logic/). Guardai la [pagina davart las mitigiaziuns da la CPU](/"
"under-the-hood/mitigations/) per la motivaziun cumpletta per mintga mancanza "
"da segirezza."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case study: Wayland compatibility"
msgstr "Studi da cas: cumpatibilitad cun Wayland"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Some detection requires less obvious sources. Modern Wayland compositors "
"like Niri strictly need 3D hardware acceleration — software rendering "
"(llvmpipe, softpipe) is not enough; the compositor will crash or refuse to "
"start."
msgstr ""
"Intginas identificaziuns dovran funtaunas main evidentas. Compositors "
"Wayland moderns sco Niri dovran absolutamain l’acceleraziun 3D cun agid da "
"la hardware – il rendering da software (llvmpipe, softpipe) na basta betg; "
"il compositor ha in collaps u refusa da s’aviar."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Rather than guess from the GPU vendor, Ditana asks the kernel which DRM "
"driver is actually active for the rendering device:"
msgstr ""
"Empè da supponer a basa dal producent da la GPU, dumonda Ditana il kernel "
"tge driver DRM ch’è propi activ per l’apparat da rendering:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"has-wayland-compatible-gpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given dir('/sys/class/drm').grep(*.basename.starts-with('renderD')).first\n"
"            { $_ ?? ($_ ~ '/device/driver').IO.resolve.basename\n"
"                    ~~ any(<amdgpu radeon i915 xe nvidia nouveau virtio-pci virtio_gpu>)\n"
"                  !! False }\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"has-wayland-compatible-gpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given dir('/sys/class/drm').grep(*.basename.starts-with('renderD')).first\n"
"            { $_ ?? ($_ ~ '/device/driver').IO.resolve.basename\n"
"                    ~~ any(<amdgpu radeon i915 xe nvidia nouveau virtio-pci virtio_gpu>)\n"
"                  !! False }\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"If your system's driver isn't on this list — `vmwgfx` in VMware, `hyperv_fb` "
"in Hyper-V, `bochs-drm` in some QEMU setups — `has-wayland-compatible-gpu` "
"evaluates to `False`. The Niri option disappears from the desktop-"
"environment selection, and Ghostty (which needs OpenGL 4.3+, unavailable to "
"software rasterizers) becomes unavailable:"
msgstr ""
"Sch’il driver da Voss sistem n’è betg sin questa glista – `vmwgfx` en "
"VMware, `hyperv_fb` en Hyper-V, `bochs-drm` en tschertas configuraziuns da "
"QEMU –, dat `has-wayland-compatible-gpu` il resultat `False`. L’opziun Niri "
"svanescha da la tscherna dal sistem da desktop, e Ghostty (che dovra OpenGL "
"4.3+, quai che programs da rendering en software na porschan betg) na stat "
"betg pli a disposiziun:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"install-ghostty\" \\\n"
"  available=\"`install-desktop-environment AND has-wayland-compatible-gpu`\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"install-ghostty\" \\\n"
"  available=\"`install-desktop-environment AND has-wayland-compatible-gpu`\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"One detector, multiple consumers. Adding a hardware-gated option later is "
"usually a single change in the consumer's `available` field — no detection "
"logic needs to be touched."
msgstr ""
"In detectur, plirs parameters che l’utiliseschan. Agiuntar pli tard "
"in’opziun che dependa da la hardware è per regla ina suletta midada en il "
"champ `available` dal parameter che utilisescha la valur – la logica "
"d’identificaziun na sto betg vegnir tutgada."
